            <div xml:id="d694">

                <pb facs="0783" n="685" xml:id="pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1491a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tenney</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-24T14:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                                1920—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>94. The Department wishes report giving all available information concerning what
                    the Chinese Government plans regarding the Chinese Eastern, with particular
                    reference to the possibility of an agreement between General Horvath and the
                    Chinese Government as to the status of that railway.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
